rs in the form \\(n = 37k + 23\\) where \\(k\\) is a non-negative integer. We need to find the largest integer \\(k\\) such that \\(n < 18,632\\).\n\nFirst, we set up the inequality:\n\\[\n37k + 23 < 18,632\n\\]\nSubtract 23 from both sides:\n\\[\n37k < 18,609\n\\]\nNext, divide both sides by 37:\n\\[\nk < \\frac{18,609}{37}\n\\]\nPerform the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{18,609}{37} \\approx 503\n\\]\nSince \\(k\\) must be an integer, the largest possible value for \\(k\\) is 503.\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"a1822eb50896fc663bd6f7ee2eb54cb99af5811e4a84b4a68f2b231f8f62c816"},"seconds":6.146078586578369,"seed":1016794342132217838,"stop":"eos","text":"Thus, \\(k\\) ranges from \\(0\\) to \\(503\\), inclusive. To find the total number of possible values for \\(k\\), we calculate:\n\\[\n503 - 0 + 1 = 504\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of whole numbers less than \\(18,632\\) that are congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\) is \\(\\boxed{504}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{504}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":true},"graded_text":"Thus, \\(k\\) ranges from \\(0\\) to \\(503\\), inclusive. To find the total number of possible values for \\(k\\), we calculate:\n\\[\n503 - 0 + 1 = 504\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of whole numbers less than \\(18,632\\) that are congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\) is \\(\\boxed{504}\\).","id":"number_theory:92"}
